    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0097" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg37"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ewing to Mr. Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-01-22"><hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 99.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 62,<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d31-f1"/> in which I communicated the request of the King of
                    the Belgians that the President of the United States would consent to act as
                    mediator in the settlement of certain questions of boundary affecting the
                    independent State of the Congo, <pb facs="0098" n="38" xml:id="pg38"/> I have
                    the honor to say that those questions were amicably settled between the Congo
                    and the French Republic by the arrangement of the 14th of August, 1894.</p>
                <p>I transmit herewith the translation of a communication which I have just received
                    from the independent State of the Congo, by which its territory is specifically
                    bounded and described.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jas. S. Ewing</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d31-a1.xml" xpointer="d31-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
